    "result_text": "Build passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the existing business-day rule in `RegistrationDates` to also skip public holidays.\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RegistrationDates.java`**\n- Added a `HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Updated the `toBusinessDay` roll-forward loop to continue past any date that is a weekend **or** a listed holiday, so it lands on the next non-holiday business day.\n- Extracted the weekend check into a small `isWeekend` helper to keep the loop condition readable.\n\nThis kept the logic in the single place both `ResolveRegistrationDate` and `EnsureDailyLimit` already share, so no rule was duplicated. `mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests green.\n\nThe acceptance test asserts the black-box invariant (default registration date is never a Saturday/Sunday) since the holiday calendar and server clock can't be driven externally, but the pinned `HOLIDAYS` set in the code now matches the one in `AcceptanceBase`.",
